 ### [Greedy Meshing](1776-greedy-meshing.md)
-Reduces rendered primitives by merging adjacent coplanar faces of identical material into larger quads. It solves the high vertex/triangle count of naive per-face rendering by minimizing draw calls. Unlike [Blocky meshing](31-blocky-meshing.md) which only culls hidden faces, greedy meshing actively expands visible faces into maximal rectangles. Choose it when reducing primitive count is more important than preserving individual voxel boundaries.
