 ## Background
-Blocky meshing methods are implemented across various rendering engines and research projects. A Java/libgdx implementation processes voxels on the CPU to build vertex and index buffers for chunk models [S1, unofficial]. An OpenGL-based renderer reduces unnecessary geometry by removing faces that would never be visible to the player, performing neighbor checks during mesh generation [S2, unofficial]. Research into radiance meshes converts tetrahedral radiance meshes into polygonal surface meshes by filtering and grouping tetrahedra based on their visual contribution [S5, unofficial].
